    {
      "question_number": "5",
      "question_text": "(2x + i)(y - 2i) = -2 - 9i",
      "diagram": null,
      "full_model_solution": "Expand: 2xy - 4xi + yi - 2i^2 = -2 - 9i => 2xy - 4xi + yi + 2 = -2 - 9i. Real: 2xy + 2 = -2 => 2xy = -4 => xy = -2. Imaginary: -4x + y = -9 => y = 4x - 9. Substitute: x(4x - 9) = -2 => 4x^2 - 9x + 2 = 0 => (x - 2)(4x - 1) = 0. So x = 2 or x = 1/4. If x = 2, y = -1. If x = 1/4, y = -8.",
